{
  "schema_version": "0.1",
  "note": "Reviewed measurement declarations, one entry per profile that carries a measured value. These replace the name-substring guessing in scripts/build_standard.py (decision D9), which produced concentrations on a probability scale and firing rates in 1/s converted from nanomolar. Each entry fixes the quantity kind (source/quantity-kinds.json), the canonical unit as a UCUM expression, and the measurement level. Prepared with AI assistance from the pre-review; every entry still needs its domain reviewer.",
  "fields": {
    "kind": "A quantity kind id from source/quantity-kinds.json.",
    "unit": "The UCUM unit the profile's positive example declares. null means the port declares its own unit and the profile fixes only the kind.",
    "scale": "nominal, ordinal, interval, ratio, proportion or count. A proportion is a part of a declared whole, which is not the same claim as a probability (decision D8).",
    "transform": "Applied transform, with its base explicit. Absent means none.",
    "requires": "Extra items this profile must require, beyond the unit, scale and quantity. Sub-paths of an array item (biological_context.intervention.route and the like) cannot be required on their own: the parent is a list, so a sub-path requirement would overwrite it. Requiring the intervention itself is the closest the v0.1 item model allows.",
    "drop_measurement": "The profile should carry no measurement at all: the value is not a quantity."
  },
